<title>ISRAEL: SOCCER-GERMANY BEAT ISRAEL 1-0 IN FRIENDLY.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-GERMANY BEAT ISRAEL 1-0 IN FRIENDLY.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany beat Israel 1-0</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0) in a friendly soccer international on Wednesday:</p>
<p>Scorer: Darius Wosz, 85th minute.</p>
<p>Attendance: 21,000</p>
<p>Israel: 1. Rafi Cohen, 2. Felix Halfon (14. Alon Hazan 68th</p>
<p>minute), 3. David Amsalem, 4. Amir Shelah, 5. Gadi Brumer, 6.</p>
<p>Ran Ben-Shimon, 7. Arik Bennado, 8. Avi Nimni, 9. Ronnie</p>
<p>Rosenthal, 10. Itzik Zohar (16. Alon Harazi 80th), 11. Eli Ohana</p>
<p>(captain) (17. Alon Mizrahi 85th).</p>
<p>Germany: 1. Oliver Kahn, 2.Markus Babbel, 3. Christian</p>
<p>Ziege, 4. Jurgen Kohler, 5. Dieter Eilts, 6. Matthias Sammer, 7.</p>
<p>Andreas Moller, 8. Mario Basler (15. Jorg Heinrich 89th), 9.</p>
<p>Jurgen Klinsmann (captain), 10. Darius Wosz, 11. Fredi Bobic</p>
<p>(17. Ulf Kirsten 46th).</p>
